          "title": "EKS Basics and When to Choose It",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What EKS Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Managed Kubernetes==: AWS runs the **control plane** (API server, etcd)",
                "You run workers: {blue:managed node groups}, {purple:self-managed nodes} or {orange:Fargate profiles}",
                "Pods call AWS APIs via ==IRSA== or **EKS Pod Identity**",
                "That is the EKS equivalent of an ECS ==task role=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Core Objects",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Object",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "==Pod==",
                  "Smallest unit"
                ],
                [
                  "==Deployment==",
                  "Replicas and rollouts"
                ],
                [
                  "==Service==",
                  "Stable virtual IP"
                ],
                [
                  "==Ingress==",
                  "HTTP routing, backed by the **AWS Load Balancer Controller**"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. ECS or EKS?",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "ECS",
                "EKS"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Pick when",
                  "AWS-only, {green:least ops}",
                  "Portability, Helm and operators, team skills"
                ],
                [
                  "Extra cost",
                  "None for control plane",
                  "Control plane fee per cluster per hour"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake: EKS for a simple app",
              "text": "You pay later in ==upgrade work== (a Kubernetes version gets ~**14 months** of support), add-ons and networking complexity."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Discovery, Load Balancers, Logs and Commands",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Discovery, Load Balancers, Logs and Commands",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Discovery and Load Balancer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Service Connect} or ==Cloud Map== gives tasks a private DNS name: `svc.namespace`",
                "Services call each other with ==no load balancer==",
                "ALB target group: type ==ip== for `awsvpc`, the service registers task IPs",
                "==healthCheckGracePeriodSeconds== delays health-check kills; a bad path kills tasks"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Internet",
                    "sub": "80 / 443",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ALB group",
                    "sub": "open to internet",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Task group",
                    "sub": "container port, source = ALB group",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Logs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`awslogs` driver in `logConfiguration` sends ==stdout and stderr== to CloudWatch",
                "Options: `awslogs-group`, `awslogs-region`, `awslogs-stream-prefix`",
                "The log group must ==already exist==",
                "Execution role needs `logs:CreateLogStream` and `logs:PutLogEvents`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday Commands",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws ecr get-login-password | docker login $ECR",
                "docker push $ECR/app:$SHA",
                "aws ecs register-task-definition --cli-input-json file://td.json",
                "aws ecs update-service --task-definition fam:rev --force-new-deployment",
                "aws ecs execute-command --task ID --interactive --command sh",
                "aws logs tail /ecs/app --follow"
              ],
              "note": "update-service points the service at a revision"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Redeploy is not rollout",
              "text": "`--force-new-deployment` alone restarts on the current revision. Add ==--task-definition fam:rev== to roll out a newly registered one."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
